From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 04:52:41 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] qualcommax: wcss-sec: don't hold firmware recovery for a
 coredump

The WCSS secure-PIL driver (pending 830-03, used on IPQ8074 and IPQ6018)
sets an inline remoteproc coredump. After a q6 firmware crash,
rproc_coredump() then waits for userspace to read the devcoredump, and
on OpenWrt nothing does: the WCSS stays stopped for the 5-minute
devcoredump timeout, with every internal radio down (hostapd keeps
reporting the BSSes as enabled meanwhile).

Seen on an IPQ6018 (Arista W-318) after a simulated firmware assert:
"stopped remote processor wcnss", then nothing for minutes; discarding
the dump by hand brought the WCSS up 0.4 s later and ath11k recovered.

Turn the coredump off by default; it can still be enabled through the
remoteproc coredump sysfs attribute.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
Link: https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/pull/26493
Signed-off-by: Robert Marko <robimarko@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit b97760cbc90505d80eafbbb4e0f683932c221c86)
---
 ...c-don-t-hold-recovery-for-a-coredump.patch | 37 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 37 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 target/linux/qualcommax/patches-6.18/0819-remoteproc-qcom-wcss-sec-don-t-hold-recovery-for-a-coredump.patch

diff --git a/target/linux/qualcommax/patches-6.18/0819-remoteproc-qcom-wcss-sec-don-t-hold-recovery-for-a-coredump.patch b/target/linux/qualcommax/patches-6.18/0819-remoteproc-qcom-wcss-sec-don-t-hold-recovery-for-a-coredump.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..70c207d742
--- /dev/null
+++ b/target/linux/qualcommax/patches-6.18/0819-remoteproc-qcom-wcss-sec-don-t-hold-recovery-for-a-coredump.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@
+From 183bb4182b696f76105052cb1cf3a4661bc20c63 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
+Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 09:16:51 -0600
+Subject: [PATCH] remoteproc: qcom: wcss-sec: don't hold recovery for a
+ coredump
+
+The driver sets an inline coredump. On a crash, rproc_coredump() then
+waits until userspace reads the devcoredump, and with no reader that
+is the devcoredump timeout: 5 minutes with the WCSS stopped, so every
+radio on it stays down. Seen on an IPQ6018 after a simulated firmware
+assert: "stopped remote processor wcnss", then nothing until the dump
+was discarded by hand; the WCSS was up 0.4 s later and ath11k
+recovered.
+
+Default to no coredump; it can still be enabled through the coredump
+sysfs attribute.
+
+Signed-off-by: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
+---
+ drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_wcss_sec.c | 6 +++++-
+ 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
+
+--- a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_wcss_sec.c
++++ b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_wcss_sec.c
+@@ -376,7 +376,11 @@ static int wcss_sec_probe(struct platfor
+ 	qcom_add_ssr_subdev(rproc, &wcss->ssr_subdev, desc->ss_name);
+ 
+ 	rproc->auto_boot = false;
+-	rproc->dump_conf = RPROC_COREDUMP_INLINE;
++	/* An inline coredump holds the recovery until userspace reads the
++	 * devcoredump, or for 5 minutes when nothing does. Leave dumps
++	 * off unless asked for through the coredump sysfs attribute.
++	 */
++	rproc->dump_conf = RPROC_COREDUMP_DISABLED;
+ 	rproc_coredump_set_elf_info(rproc, ELFCLASS32, EM_NONE);
+ 
+ 	if (desc->use_tmelcom) {
